  3.97877484028648*^9}, {3.9787749904269123`*^9, 3.9787750094166317`*^9}, {
  3.978775090781111*^9, 3.9787751128555756`*^9}},
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"e87816e0-a9f2-4ec9-a8a2-32272dfb6314"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Bigger Bang:\nQuestion:  ",
 StyleBox["Are Universe (s) of  masses  \[PlusMinus] M  created in pairs  at  \
time x4 = 0\n(before  the  particles  of  the  standard  model  exist) ?",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.93, 0.27, 0.27]]
}], "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.974736985236294*^9, 3.9747370119622383`*^9}, {
   3.974737048968073*^9, 3.9747370716103935`*^9}, {3.9751366097437057`*^9, 
   3.975136708455105*^9}, {3.975223987038294*^9, 3.975223997896761*^9}, 
   3.975224058333971*^9},
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"0e29ac9a-51da-4f6d-872e-0bf2b5c153e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Scratch work", "Title",
  FontSize->24],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["Patrick L. Nash, Ph.D.",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["\n",
  FontSize->18,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["(c) 2022, under GPL\nProfessor, UTSA Physics and Astronomy, \
Retired (UTSA)\nPatrick299Nash  at    gmail   ...\nDo not read if you are \
irascible; I apologize for typos  and  duplications  and ....\ngit clone \
https://github.com/43d168f3e/Eternal-DEFLATION-Inflation.git\n\
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]git@github.com:43d168f3e/Eternal-DEFLATION-Inflation.\
git\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]\n\n\nEver wonder why there are  3 space \
dimensions and  1  time dimension?  \nEver wonder if   Nature  loves  the \
norm  relation \:2016XY\:2016 = \:2016X\:2016\:2016Y\:2016, for  X, Y \
\[Element] Nature?\n\nWell, Hurwitz\[CloseCurlyQuote]s theorem  says  that  \
there  are  only  4 normed division algebras (\:2016XY\:2016=\:2016X\:2016\
\:2016Y\:2016) over the real numbers, which, up to isomorphism,  are   the  \
1-dim (over \[DoubleStruckCapitalR]) real numbers  \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalR],the   2-dim  complex numbers,the   4-dim   \
quaternions, and the  8-dim   octonions.\n\nSince  this   is   the   age  of  \
  the  Xtreme,   let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s   go   with   the    8-dim   \
octonions.    Actually   the   split   octonions, in this notebook,    with   \
4   space    dimensions   and   4   time   dimensions.\n\nThe origin of this \
calculation has its roots in \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]A Remarkable \
Representation of the 3+2 de Sitter Group\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] by \
P.A.M.Dirac, J.Math.Phys.4,901\[Dash]909 (1963). \n\nComment:  The term \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]reduced Brauer\[Dash]Weyl generators\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote],  below, refers to a specific set of irreducible \
generators for certain complex Clifford algebras, particularly in the context \
of mathematical physics and the study of Dirac \
spinors.\[NonBreakingSpace]These generators were introduced by ",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["E.A. Lord",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 StyleBox[" (E. A. Lord. \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]The Dirac spinor in six \
dimensions\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. Mathematical Proceedings of the Cambridge \
Philosophical Society, vol. 64, pp. 765\[Dash]778, 1968) and are described as \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]reduced\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] because they form an \
irreducible representation of the Clifford algebra   ",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalC]", 
    RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0],ExpressionUUID->
  "8c7aaa64-58df-411e-b4ae-44e3acf0d28a"],
 StyleBox["  from   ",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalC]", 
    RowBox[{"2", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"n", "-", "1"}], ")"}]}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0],ExpressionUUID->
  "7d7a4ede-da4b-42ab-aaa0-561f4f93c943"],
 StyleBox["\[NonBreakingSpace].\n\nHere,  we employ  Lord\[CloseCurlyQuote]s  \
idea of reduced Brauer\[Dash]Weyl generators to extend \
Dirac\[CloseCurlyQuote]s 4\[Times]4 gamma matrices into  this notebook\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s  real tau8  8\[Times]8 and  tau16   16\[Times]16 \
matrices,\nwhich  are  employed  to write  down the \[OpenCurlyQuote]Dirac \
Equation  for the Universe\[CloseCurlyQuote],\n[remember, this is before  the \
 particles  of  the  standard  model  exist ]\n  formulated  in  terms  of a  \
 ",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"O", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"4", ",", "4"}], ")"}]}], "_"], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"80e0d93b-1c34-4167-a87b-d5ce8fcf8c5a"],
 StyleBox[" spinor \[CapitalPsi]16\n(\[CapitalPsi]16  AKA \[OpenCurlyQuote]",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["WAVE FUNCTION OF  the UNIVERSE,\[CloseCurlyQuote]",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.93, 0.27, 0.27]],
 StyleBox[" which could possibly be named something more pompous).\nThen this \
equation is used to \n[WARNING: syncope, presyncope AHEAD]\ncouple the ",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["WAVE FUNCTION OF the UNIVERSE",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.93, 0.27, 0.27]],
 StyleBox["  to  Gravity.\n\n",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["THIS  WORK  IS PARTIALLY  BASED  ON :",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.8, 0.3, 0.8]],
 StyleBox["\n",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 Cell[BoxData[
  GraphicsBox[
   TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["
